```java
abstract class Shape {                 // ABSTRACTION: contract
    private String color;              // ENCAPSULATION: private state
    public String getColor() { return color; }
    public abstract double area();     // subclasses define 'how'
}

class Circle extends Shape {           // INHERITANCE: IS-A Shape
    private final double r;
    Circle(double r) { this.r = r; }
    public double area() { return Math.PI * r * r; } // POLYMORPHISM: override
}

Shape s = new Circle(2);               // parent reference, child object
System.out.println(s.area());          // runtime dispatch to Circle.area()
```

```java
class Printer {
    void print(int x)    { System.out.println("int: " + x); }
    void print(String s) { System.out.println("str: " + s); }
    void print(int x, int y) { System.out.println(x + "," + y); }
}
new Printer().print(5);      // compiler picks print(int) at compile time
new Printer().print("hi");  // compiler picks print(String)
```

```java
class Animal { String sound() { return "..."; } }
class Dog extends Animal {
    @Override String sound() { return "Woof"; } // same signature
}
Animal a = new Dog();        // reference type Animal, object Dog
System.out.println(a.sound()); // "Woof" — JVM dispatches at runtime
```

```java
String a = new String("hi");
String b = new String("hi");
if (a == b) { /* never runs: different objects */ }
else        { System.out.println("== says NOT equal"); } // prints

String user = readInput();     // runtime value, not interned
if (user == "admin") { /* fails even when user is "admin" */ }
```

```java
String a = new String("hi");
String b = new String("hi");
System.out.println(a.equals(b)); // true — same content

String user = readInput();
if ("admin".equals(user)) { /* correct, and null-safe */ }
```
*Calling `.equals()` on the literal (`"admin".equals(user)`) also avoids a `NullPointerException` when `user` is null.*

```java
interface Auditable {                 // a CAN-DO capability
    String audit();                   // contract
    default void log() { System.out.println(audit()); } // Java 8 default
}
// Unrelated types can all be Auditable:
class Employee implements Auditable { public String audit() { return "emp"; } }
class Invoice  implements Auditable { public String audit() { return "inv"; } }
```
*A class can implement many interfaces (`class X implements Auditable, Comparable<X>`) but extend only one class.*

```java
// Reusing Stack methods, but a Queue is NOT a Stack (IS-A fails)
class Queue extends java.util.Stack<Integer> {
    void enqueue(int x) { push(x); }
}
Queue q = new Queue();
q.push(1);              // inherited — leaks Stack's whole API
q.pop();                // callers can break queue semantics
```

```java
class Queue {
    private final Deque<Integer> data = new ArrayDeque<>(); // HAS-A
    void enqueue(int x) { data.addLast(x); }   // delegate
    int  dequeue()      { return data.removeFirst(); }
}
// Only queue operations are exposed; the backing store can change freely.
```
*Composition hides the helper's API and lets you swap `ArrayDeque` for another structure without affecting callers.*

```java
interface PaymentProcessor {            // ABSTRACTION
    void process(Order order);
}

class CardProcessor implements PaymentProcessor { // INHERITANCE (implements)
    private final String apiKey;        // ENCAPSULATION: hidden, validated
    CardProcessor(String apiKey) {
        if (apiKey == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("key required");
        this.apiKey = apiKey;
    }
    public void process(Order o) { /* charge card using apiKey */ }
}

class CheckoutService {
    void checkout(Order o, PaymentProcessor p) {
        p.process(o);                   // POLYMORPHISM: runtime dispatch
    }
}
// Add UpiProcessor or ApplePayProcessor later — CheckoutService never changes.
```
